# Transee mobile app configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) or set these in your build environment.
#
# SECURITY: every EXPO_PUBLIC_* value is inlined into the JavaScript bundle at
# build time and is readable by anyone with the APK. Only public, non-secret
# values may live here. The Azure Translator key is NEVER one of them — it
# belongs solely to the backend's own environment. See server/.env.example.

# This file is for LOCAL development only. EAS builds never see it: they run on
# EAS's own machines and take their values from the EAS environment matching the
# build profile. Set those with `eas env:create` — see the README — and keep the
# placeholder below empty, so no deployment URL is ever committed.
#
# The value is inlined into the bundle at build time, so changing it always
# needs a new build. There is no runtime override.

# Public base URL of the Transee backend, with no trailing slash.
# This is the Transee API, not an Azure endpoint.
# Leave unset to build without online translation; the app then reports
# "no translation engine is available" rather than inventing a result.
EXPO_PUBLIC_TRANSEE_API_URL=
